From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:14:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/43] Shaders: view-address table for descriptors picked by a
 computed index

A program that loads a buffer descriptor at an index it computes, and only
uses the descriptor's address as data, found no root view to ask and was
refused ("a descriptor read only as data"). The host now keeps one table of
the title addresses of the heap's buffer views by heap slot (SLOT_VIEWS, a
root SRV like SLOT_STRIDES, 2^21 slots x 16 bytes), filled where a slot is
written, and the lowering reads the address, length and stride from it.
A computed term in a used descriptor's address takes the same table.

Adapted from uiliannn/VItoriaBr commits b62bbc0 and 77ad907 (GPL-3.0, the
fork's own licence); the draw.rs part is rewritten for the current main,
the rest applies unchanged.

Co-authored-by: uiliannn
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit a1855ac872b3fb743177ee975aadd3e099da9626)
